WHAT CHANGED FROM e9508660 — ONE EXPRESSION
  The L-C assert's ANCHOR COMPONENT now covers picks 1-64 only. The pool slot (65) is not a fit
  input: no pool row teaches the lens, and no pool row reads the surface (pool rows are excluded from
  `real`, never enter _V0CURVE, and take _v0_raw through v0_start's fall-through).

  TWO DEFECTS THIS REMOVES, both the seam's catch:
   1. A NAME TRAP. The component was a look-alike of the census payload that WAS NOT the census
      payload — it read 5c1ff693 where the ladder's own identity is e69a3f38. Restricted, the
      component IS e69a3f38 verbatim, so the key can be read against the census without translation.
   2. A SPURIOUS INAPPLICABLE AT THE LANDING. N43 moves the pool level. Under the old expression that
      would have changed the anchor component, changed the key, and made the assert report
      INAPPLICABLE at exactly the moment it is most needed — while the ladder the lens actually uses
      had not moved at all. A guard that goes quiet when the system changes around it is the failure
      mode this leg exists to refuse.

  The lens digest is UNCHANGED (b760b17ea3ab76acdad81bf87f2b90ad): the fit did not move, only the
  key's anchor component. That is the check that this was a keying fix and not a silent re-fit.

  The superseded key (…|5c1ff693|…) is REMOVED rather than left beside the new one: it is
  unreachable under the corrected expression, and a dead expectation nobody can reproduce is
  clutter that reads like evidence.

